---
description: Do not rebuild scrollable lists when only the selected row changes
alwaysApply: true
---

# List selection must not jump scroll

**Anti-pattern:** on row click, call `listEl.empty()` / rebuild the whole list so the selected item gets `is-selected`. That resets `scrollTop` and often leaves the selected row at the bottom of the viewport.

**Do instead:**

1. Keep the existing DOM rows on selection.
2. Toggle `is-selected` (and buttons that depend on selection) in place — see `openDoc` in `obsidian/src/library-view.js`, `syncListSelection` in campaign/homebrew views.
3. Rebuild the list only when its *contents* change (filter, tab, create, delete, reload).
4. If a rebuild is required, save and restore `scrollTop` around `empty()`.

Applies to library rows, campaign notes, homebrew entries, encounter rosters, and any similar scrollable hit list under `obsidian/`.
